The ATS integrations were written against the vendors' documented public JSON
endpoints (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby) and contain no third-party code.

autopilot-jobhunt (https://github.com/tarunlnmiit/autopilot-jobhunt, MIT) was
evaluated during design and informed the module layout, but no code or data from
it was used.

career-ops (https://github.com/career-ops-hq/career-ops, MIT) — the dedupe rules, the liveness classifier, the salary text rules and the follow-up cadence (nudges at 7 d, then 7 d apart, max 2, then cold; replied 1 d then 3 d; interview thank-you at 1 d) are reimplemented from its ideas; no code copied verbatim. Ideas ported as well: the Greenhouse questions endpoint, the obstacle checks and the submit-control detector, the outreach personas and the 200-character connection-note limit.

JobSpy (https://github.com/speedyapply/JobSpy, MIT) is a dependency, used to read LinkedIn and Indeed listings.
